  (text "The following topology represented in the schematic \nillustrates the connections and basic working \nof the PCB."
    (at 177.8 55.88 0)
    (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 0223eeb6-e190-4162-a5df-d6769968160f)
  )
  (text "The regulated power supply is also used for \nthe reset and enable circuitry of the STM32. \nA switch is provided to manually control the \nreset/enable function, allowing the ESP32 to \nbe restarted or enabled when required."
    (at 78.74 171.45 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 14b5c7d0-5821-4571-85c6-4f9d06f8fd01)
  )
  (text "Additional GPIO pins of the ESP32-S3 are \nexposed through external headers. \nThese pins can be used to connect various \nexternal sensors, actuators, or other peripherals \nas required for different applications."
    (at 146.05 157.48 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 28928f4a-b52a-4001-9c9e-aeda40773762)
  )
  (text "The same USB connection provides a 5 V power \nsupply to the PCB. This 5 V input is regulated \nthrough the AMS1117 voltage regulator, \nwhich converts it to 3.3 V to power the \nESP32-S3 and other required circuitry."
    (at 64.77 93.98 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 5a0a1d82-534d-421e-a078-cb7d3bef0a58)
  )
  (text "The USB interface is used to connect the PCB \nto an external device, such as a laptop, for \ndata communication with the ESP32-S3. \nIt also allows the firmware/code to be uploaded\ndirectly to the ESP32-S3 board."
    (at 149.86 81.28 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 6c9cb10f-05f6-459c-b70e-4929c73c3036)
  )
  (text "Tolopogy_and_sheets" (at 187.96 190.5 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid c4beac83-70c8-44d5-8633-1982fd31eb69)
  )
  (text "An LED is directly connected to Pin 14 of the \nESP32.This LED can be controlled through the \nfirmware and is used to verify the proper \noperation of the microcontroller after the \ncode has been uploaded."
    (at 149.86 97.79 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid c62377ee-eb96-40f9-9c89-8fc1deddef10)
  )

